WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.417
- Thanks to Trade Coffee for keeping

00:00:01.417 --> 00:00:02.420
"Legal Eagle" in the air,

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:03.690
'cause you would not want to see me

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.730
before my first cup of joe, am I right?

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:08.890
Ugh, all right, let's
watch "Tiger King" again.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:09.790
- [Lawyer] Where's the film?

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:11.880
- [Joe] In my recording studio.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.260
- [Lawyer] And they don't
have copies of it or anything?

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.093
- [Joe] No.

00:00:17.045 --> 00:00:18.078
- [Lawyer] Do you see
what I'm saying, Joe?

00:00:18.078 --> 00:00:19.730
- [Joe] I hear you.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:21.500
- Don't record your lawyer.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.950
Do not record your lawyer
without permission.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:27.402
I cannot emphasize that highly enough.

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:31.220
(lighthearted music)

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:34.970
Hey all you cats and kittens,
I mean legal eagles. (beeps)

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.990
I told you, this one almost broke me

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:40.140
but you guys had a lot
of unanswered questions.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.140
Just when I thought I was
out, you pull me back in.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.810
But I wanted to cover
some of the other things

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:46.927
that I left out in the original

00:00:46.927 --> 00:00:48.650
"Real Lawyer Reacts to Tiger King,"

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:51.080
some of the other crimes committed

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.830
allegedly, allegedly, in the documentary,

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.730
and some of the other
crimes that the characters

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.730
definitely committed offscreen.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.990
Look, if Joel McHale can squeeze out

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:01.410
an eighth episode of "Tiger King"

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.770
with an iPhone and AirPods
in his ears the whole time,

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:07.520
we can do a second episode
of "Real Lawyer Reacts."

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:10.810
So without further ado,
let's dig in to "Tiger King"

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:13.160
again for some reason.

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:15.800
- The last day that I saw Don,

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.090
he told me that he was done,

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.140
that he was divorcing her,

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:21.760
that she was one of the worst people

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.000
he'd ever met in his life,
and she was very dangerous.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.720
- He indicated to me that he was

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:30.823
going to tell Carole
that he wanted a divorce.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.490
Never saw him again.

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:34.710
- Okay, so right off the bat,

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:36.600
probably the biggest question I got was

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.460
did I think that Carole
Baskin committed murder?

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:41.680
On this channel, I tend to avoid

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:43.580
trying to make judgment calls like these

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.030
when not all of the facts are known.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:48.090
Sometimes I will go out on a limb

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:50.150
and I will give my opinion as to whether

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:51.260
I think a crime was committed

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:54.000
or whether a lawsuit
is meritorious or not,

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.920
but almost always that's in
cases where most of the facts,

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.090
if not all of the facts, are known.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:00.040
Like for example a copyright case

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:04.140
where I can look at the
allegedly infringing piece of art

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:05.390
and the original piece of art,

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:09.350
and I don't need to know
more facts than that.

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:10.510
And that's really all that's relevant

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:11.800
in a copyright case, for example.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:16.180
But here, this is a one-sided
documentary with an agenda.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.740
I don't know that anyone
can really opine on this.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.570
I will say that in doing more research

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:23.060
for this episode and the prior episode,

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.320
there's a lot more information

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.560
about Don's medical diagnosis,

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:29.440
about his Alzheimer's
and his bipolar disorder.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:33.340
There's a lot more in terms
of the conservatorship cases

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.960
between him and his former family.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.660
So there are a lot of facts out there

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:38.810
that are not in the documentary

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.200
that I think are probably relevant here

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.790
that I think paint things
in a different light.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.430
And the documentary needs to have

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:46.610
equal parties opposing each
other for narrative purposes.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:48.090
You need to have a good guy and a bad guy

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:49.640
or a bad guy and another bad guy

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.570
of relatively equal power,

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:53.560
and that lends to the narrative.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.410
So I would say if you're
interested in this,

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:59.510
check out Carole Baskin's
retort to the documentary.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.470
She puts out a lot of
additional facts out there,

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.730
it's on the Big Cat Rescue's website,

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.530
and judge for yourself.

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:06.880
But I don't think it's my place

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:10.030
to opine on whether I think Carole Baskin

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:11.920
killed her former husband.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.760
I will say, though, that
between Joe and Carole Baskin,

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.940
only one of those people
is in federal prison

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:20.700
with a potentially life
sentence to serve out.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.550
So take that as you will

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:25.430
and you decide who deserves
the benefit of the doubt there.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:30.220
- [Joe] My producers are
filming a reality show.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:31.720
- [Lawyer] So they wanna do a show

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:34.402
related to your park up there?

00:03:34.402 --> 00:03:35.932
- [Joe] They actually got it filmed.

00:03:35.932 --> 00:03:37.609
- Do they?
- Uh-huh.

00:03:37.609 --> 00:03:40.033
- [Lawyer] And how are
you protecting that?

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:41.380
- [Joe] What do you mean?

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:42.353
- [Lawyer] Well, if they've got it filmed,

00:03:42.353 --> 00:03:44.740
what do they need you for?

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:49.200
- He blew up so bad when I
showed him that contract.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.750
He was like, "You don't own me."

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.387
I said, "Joe, actually, I do right now.

00:03:53.387 --> 00:03:56.017
"I do own this show, I do own it."

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:57.850
- [Lawyer] Where is the film?

00:03:57.850 --> 00:03:59.940
- [Joe] In my recording studio.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.946
- [Lawyer] And they don't
have copies up here?

00:04:01.946 --> 00:04:02.863
- [Joe] No.

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:05.877
- [Lawyer] You see what I'm saying, Joe?

00:04:05.877 --> 00:04:07.800
- [Joe] Yeah, I hear you.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.560
- Don't record your lawyer.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:13.010
Do not record your lawyer
without permission.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.410
I cannot emphasize that highly enough.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:17.300
There's really no reason for Joe

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:18.810
to have recorded this in the first place.

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:20.290
Number one, if you record it

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:21.880
and then you show it to somebody else,

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:24.550
you are waiving the
attorney-client privilege.

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:28.150
You are removing the
confidence of the discussion

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:30.020
between you and your attorney,

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:33.190
and therefore third parties can get access

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:36.120
to the things that you
discussed during that meeting.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:39.390
On top of that, without permission,

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:41.130
if this is a one party consent state,

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.580
you might be violating
their right to privacy.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:46.450
On top of that, you have evidence

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:48.320
that is bad for both of you

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.640
because if indeed the lawyer is suggesting

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.930
that you go out and commit a crime,

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:57.640
that might qualify as
conspiracy to commit arson.

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:00.300
Lawyers have an ethical obligation

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.920
to inform law enforcement when they know

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.790
that a crime is going to be committed,

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:07.460
so that goes beyond the realm

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:09.360
of attorney-client privilege
in the first place.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:12.320
Now obviously we don't know
exactly what's going on here.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:14.770
This footage, I think,
is pretty chopped up.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:16.750
It's meant to imply that something

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.270
nefarious is going on
between Joe and his attorney,

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:20.780
so we don't know exactly
what was discussed.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:22.470
But the implication is that the lawyer

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:25.120
is suggesting that he
go out and commit arson.

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:26.790
There's no attorney-client privilege

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:29.510
that's going to attach
when you actively suggest

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:32.730
to a client that they go
out and commit a crime.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:35.880
There are very, very,
very big problems here.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:39.660
- That building, where
the alligators were kept,

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:42.630
as well as a studio that Joe had,

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:45.363
it was clearly an arson,
it was a set fire.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:51.090
- It had burned so hot,
there was nothing left.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:53.020
I dropped to my knees and I cried.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:55.780
- Okay, just as I am not going to opine

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:59.200
on whether I think Carole Baskin
killed her former husband,

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.220
I'm not going to opine on who I think

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:02.990
committed the arson here.

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:06.410
This is, I think, based on what
is shown in the documentary

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:08.420
clearly an act of arson.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:09.410
It doesn't seem like there's any

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:11.600
natural reason why this
thing would catch fire.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.690
And there are people with definite motives

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:16.120
as to why they might commit arson.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:18.290
What I will say, though, is that

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:22.870
if one sets fire to their
own property intentionally,

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:25.270
that still qualifies as arson.

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:27.640
So you can't just go around
torching your own stuff

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:30.090
because obviously that can
create negative externalities

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.380
and you might catch your neighbor's

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:34.770
alligator enclosure on fire as well.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:37.700
So we don't want all of
their stuff burning down too,

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:40.520
so if you set fire to your own barn,

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:42.960
that qualifies as arson, don't do that.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.150
- So I'm Dr. Bhagavan Antle.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:49.090
B-H-A-G-A-V-A-N Antle, A-N-T-L-E.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:50.900
Dr. Bhagavan Antle.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:53.290
- Okay, let's talk about Doc Antle.

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:56.140
There are two really interesting
things about Doc Antle.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.110
Number one is that everyone was curious

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:00.640
about potential sexual harassment claims

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:02.580
based on the sort of implied

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:05.820
cult-like behavior at this institution.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:10.080
- If they wanted to get
to the top really quickly,

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:11.300
they should sleep with him.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.870
- In general, there are two
kinds of sexual harassment.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.620
There's quid pro quo sexual harassment

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.380
and then there's hostile
workplace environment.

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:20.570
Quid pro quo is do
something of a sexual nature

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:23.440
for me and you'll either be rewarded

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:25.853
or you'll be punished
if you don't do this.

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:29.600
- He controlled every aspect of our day.

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:30.950
What we were allowed to do.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.950
Definitely what we were
allowed to eat as vegetarians

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:37.810
but also they were pushing
me to get implants.

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:39.110
- And then the hostile work environment

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:42.760
is using the basis of sex to create

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:44.170
some hostile work environment.

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:46.590
And you can imagine that
if you are pressuring women

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:49.440
to have plastic surgery, that
could certainly give rise

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:51.420
to a hostile work environment

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:54.460
and give rise to a
sexual harassment claim.

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:56.550
Now the other really interesting
thing about Doc Antle

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:58.840
is that his compound in South Carolina

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:02.970
was raided by the police
in December of 2019.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.490
Now, Antle claims that the warrants

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:07.550
had to do with tracing lions

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:11.040
that ended up in his institution

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:15.560
that came from a park of very ill repute,

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:18.580
and that the police were just simply

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:21.990
trying to track down information
related to somebody else.

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:24.400
The police are not saying why it is

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.880
that they raided his park.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:28.210
As you can imagine, they are not likely

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:31.160
to comment on an ongoing investigation.

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:33.140
But it's sort of up to you as to

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:35.240
whether you think that it's related

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:40.240
to Doc Antle's own improper
conduct regarding animals,

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:42.960
or it's related to somebody else, or both.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.520
But again, we don't
have all the facts here.

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:46.710
- [Lawyer] It doesn't show stalking,

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:47.680
it doesn't show battery.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:48.930
It doesn't show anything.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:50.670
It shows a verbal argument,

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:52.880
and that's not enough
to get an injunction.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.970
- [Don] And so that's why
you think it was denied.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:56.820
- That's why I know it was denied.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:57.653
- [Don] But obviously--

00:08:57.653 --> 00:08:58.840
- That was dead on arrival.

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:01.780
What raises my eyebrows is
she threatened to kill me.

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:03.180
- [Don] And that's not enough to get a--

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:04.050
- Nope.

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:04.883
- A restraining order?
- It's free speech.

00:09:04.883 --> 00:09:06.210
There's free speech.

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:08.320
We don't restrain free
speech in this country,

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:10.490
we punish it after it's done.

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:13.190
- Got a lot of questions
about Don's attempt

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:15.030
to get a restraining order

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:18.270
and the attorney's comments
that it was just free speech,

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:21.660
so we punish speech after the fact

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:23.960
instead of getting restraining
orders ahead of time,

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:26.890
and that's, it's very half right.

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:28.120
It's maybe a quarter right.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:29.910
Now, first of all, in Florida

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:32.260
you can get a domestic restraining order,

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:36.030
and it doesn't require an
actual act of physical abuse.

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:37.250
In Florida, a restraining order

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:39.520
is generally known as an
injunction for protection.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:42.950
It's a civil court order,
but if you violate that order

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:45.860
that can lead to a criminal offense.

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:48.390
It does not require violence.

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:52.810
You can get it if there's
a history of abuse

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:57.690
or they're real, credible threats.

00:09:57.690 --> 00:09:59.380
And generally speaking, there's a thing

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:01.970
under First Amendment
law called a true threat,

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:04.170
which is not protected
by the First Amendment.

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:07.420
So you can't go around
making true threats to people

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:10.130
and thinking that you're
going to escape liability.

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:12.610
So it is possible for Don
to get a restraining order

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.460
under these circumstances,
but you can imagine

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:18.820
where that is simply generalized threats,

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:20.210
it would be difficult.

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:23.200
Oh, and speaking of restraining orders,

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.130
Don wasn't the only one who wanted

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:27.160
to get a restraining order.

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:31.180
Joe's ex-husband, John
Finlay, has a history

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:33.340
of some criminal activity,

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:35.900
including in 2014 he was arrested

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.660
for domestic assault and battery

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:39.840
when he reportedly attacked Joe,

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:41.310
although he was never charged.

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:43.420
And months later, in October of 2014,

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:46.510
Finlay filed for a
protective order against Joe,

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:49.330
but that protective
order was also dismissed

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:51.720
because he failed to
meet his burden of proof.

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:53.880
And in September of 2018,

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:56.010
the mother of his young daughter

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:57.780
filed for a petition
for a protective order

00:10:57.780 --> 00:10:59.990
against John Finlay himself.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:02.240
So a lot of protective
orders going around,

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:04.000
a lot of potential assault and battery.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:06.140
It's a really sad
situation, unfortunately.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:09.050
- With Jeff Lowe coming in to help him

00:11:09.050 --> 00:11:12.410
Joe believed that if he just convinced us

00:11:12.410 --> 00:11:15.350
that he had endless resources
to keep the lawsuit going,

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:17.570
we would suddenly fold
our tent and go away,

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:20.210
which of course we were not going to do.

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:24.100
- [Joe] My lawyers recommended
that we just dissolve

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:26.920
the Garold Wayne Interactive Zoo company

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:29.430
and let Jeff open one in his name

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:32.770
so Carole would have to start
the lawsuits all over again.

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:34.910
- Ah, Jeff Lowe.

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:36.890
What can be said about Jeff Lowe?

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:40.810
I would've thought he
dressed really cool in 1997.

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:44.210
So initially when I saw
this potential investment

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:47.010
from Jeff Lowe into Joe's zoo,

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:49.540
it sounded like another
fraudulent transfer.

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:51.930
We talked about, in the prior episode,

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:53.630
about the fraudulent transfer

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:56.920
between Joe and his mother,
Shirley Schreibvogel,

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:59.210
which we know it was a fraudulent transfer

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:01.260
because she admitted as much.

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:02.850
He was trying to hide his assets

00:12:02.850 --> 00:12:05.460
by putting them in the
name of somebody else,

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:07.330
which, don't do that.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.580
So if you wanna hear all about
that fraudulent transfer,

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:12.270
check out "Real Lawyer Reacts
to Tiger King Part 01."

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:13.930
I'll put a link in the description.

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:15.100
But it sounded like Jeff Lowe

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:16.300
was doing the exact same thing.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:19.020
He was taking title to the zoo

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:22.410
in an effort to prevent Carole Baskin

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:24.590
from getting the assets of the zoo.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:26.340
It seems like he's done
more than that, though.

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:28.660
It sounds like he's made
a material investment

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:29.870
into the zoo itself.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:31.450
I don't have all the facts here,

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:34.090
but it sounds like this
may be more bonafide

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:36.600
than the transfer to Joe's mother.

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:39.650
So I didn't think we can necessarily

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:43.140
say Jeff Lowe committed a
fraudulent transfer here.

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:45.773
And given that he's actively
running the zoo itself,

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:48.440
he had to make some sort of investment.

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:50.180
It's hard to do, but it's not impossible

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:53.350
to invest in distressed assets like this

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:55.530
without it being a fraudulent transfer.

00:12:55.530 --> 00:12:57.820
- He decided he wants to stay in Vegas

00:12:57.820 --> 00:12:59.940
and try and make money out there.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:01.690
He talked a sponsor into buying a bus

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:04.080
and they called it the Jungle Bus.

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:06.550
- [Saff] Like a party bus with animals.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:07.383
- Why?

00:13:07.383 --> 00:13:08.870
- [Reinke] They haul people
from casino to casino

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:11.280
and let them play with cubs
while they're doing it.

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:14.620
- We thought it would be a
good idea, but we were wrong.

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:16.400
That was a big (beep) mistake.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:18.660
- Huh, yeah, so even if we give

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:20.280
Jeff Lowe the benefit of the doubt

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:22.560
with respect to the G.W. Zoo,

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:24.130
I'm not sure we can give
him the benefit of the doubt

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:27.500
with respect to his Vegas business.

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.720
According to court
documents, Mr. Lowe faces

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:32.220
open court cases in Las
Vegas Municipal Court

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:33.540
where he's accused of doing business

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.310
without a license in 2017,

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:37.780
and failing to obtain a license or permit

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:39.670
for wild or farm animals.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:42.330
So I can't imagine why adding big cats

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:45.580
to a shuttle service
for drunk Vegas tourists

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:46.640
wouldn't work out.

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:49.240
Seems like a really,
really bad investment.

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:51.670
But a good investment would be
to subscribe to this channel.

00:13:51.670 --> 00:13:53.620
In fact, I was checking
my Google Analytics

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:57.120
and only 30% of the people
that watch this channel

00:13:57.120 --> 00:13:58.310
are subscribed to this channel.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:01.160
So please subscribe if
you like this content.

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:03.440
And if you click the notification bell,

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:04.860
I'm in the comments for the first hour

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.090
after I release a video.

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:08.120
So you can ask me all of the rest

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:10.600
of the crazy questions we
have about "Tiger King."

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:12.480
Ah, (beep) my life.

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:15.090
And it probably won't surprise
you to learn that Jeff Lowe

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:18.200
also has pleaded guilty
to mail and wire fraud.

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:20.230
- Saff, you identify as a man.

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:21.770
Were you upset when they kept

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:23.810
referring to you as she on the show?

00:14:23.810 --> 00:14:25.070
- I don't think it bothered me

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:27.350
as much as it bothered everyone else.

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:28.950
I didn't really pay it any mind.

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:30.580
- Okay, let's talk about Saff.

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:32.080
Apparently in the original documentary,

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:34.670
the documentarians misgendered Saff.

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:36.380
I was using female pronouns

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:37.770
and apparently that's not correct,

00:14:37.770 --> 00:14:40.140
so I apologize for that miscommunication.

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:42.380
I guess that was cleared
up in the eighth episode

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:43.710
which I hadn't seen by the time

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:46.110
that I did the first episode
of "Real Lawyer Reacts."

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:48.800
But regardless, Saff is
a pretty tough cookie

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:52.470
given that they were
able to get back to work

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:54.700
after getting their arm ripped off.

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:56.440
- Who would you trust first again:

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:59.510
Joe Exotic or the tiger
who bit your arm off?

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:00.370
- The tiger.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.640
- Saff also has a bit
of a checkered history

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:06.090
including being arrested
at least eight times

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:08.900
by the Garvin County,
Oklahoma Sheriff's Department,

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:11.170
including charges for
DUI, carrying weapons,

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:13.290
obtaining goods with a false premise,

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:15.190
and failure to appear for warrants.

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:20.120
So yeah, tough cookie and a
checkered history as well.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:21.940
- Well, Joe came to me one
day just out of the blue.

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:23.930
He says, "You think Allen
could kill somebody?"

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:25.340
I said, "Is he capable of it?"

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:27.670
And I said, "Of course, who's not?"

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:30.327
- I said, "I'll cut her (beep)
head of for you if you want."

00:15:30.327 --> 00:15:32.797
And he was all into that.

00:15:32.797 --> 00:15:35.147
I said, "Would you like
me to bring it back?"

00:15:35.147 --> 00:15:37.636
"No, no, get rid of it in the swamp!"

00:15:37.636 --> 00:15:41.910
I was like, "Okay, will do."

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:43.240
- Frank Allen Glover.

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:46.550
He seems like such a normal, nice guy.

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:49.660
A lot of people had
questions about his plea deal

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:50.880
and his prior history.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:54.100
Allen Glover has been
arrested at least 20 times

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:56.170
including DUI, domestic violence,

00:15:56.170 --> 00:15:58.270
possession of drugs,
and assault and battery.

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:00.780
Like you name it, this guy has
basically been accused of it.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:03.200
So given this guy's past history,

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:05.820
they were surprised
that he was not charged

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:09.300
in the same conspiracy to
murder that Joe Exotic was.

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:13.290
And prosecutors and US
attorneys have a lot of leeway

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:15.660
in terms of who they will charge and why.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:17.530
And coopering with the government

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:20.460
is a great way to get a
reduction in your sentence,

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:25.040
to get a reduction down
to suspended probation,

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:27.540
or sometimes not being
even charged at all.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:29.610
Now it's a weird interplay between

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:32.230
the way that this works
in the federal system,

00:16:32.230 --> 00:16:34.600
where there are sentencing
guidelines that,

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:37.220
try as you might, the
prosecutors have less leeway

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:41.730
in terms of being able to forgive people

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:43.940
based on their cooperation
with the government.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:45.860
Now, the way that they
tend to get around that

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:47.277
is that instead of saying,

00:16:47.277 --> 00:16:50.137
"You were charged with
conspiracy to commit murder,

00:16:50.137 --> 00:16:52.980
"and we're only gonna give
you probation for that,"

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:55.430
that generally doesn't work
under the sentencing guidelines.

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:58.410
They simply only charge him
with a lesser included crime,

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:02.200
something that can be
pled down to no jail time

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:03.830
or some other suspended sentence.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:06.180
So I suspect that is what happened here,

00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:07.910
that they just simply didn't charge him

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:11.080
with the same crime that
Joe Exotic was charged with,

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:14.420
and they went for the maximum
penalty for Joe Exotic

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:16.670
because he was the sort of mastermind

00:17:16.670 --> 00:17:19.650
and the one that they
really wanted to take down

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:22.540
based on the egregiousness
of his behavior.

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:26.940
- You forged my name 20
(beep) times on cashed checks.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.210
Just in that 12 months,
while he was running

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:31.880
for the Governor of Oklahoma,

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:35.360
we found, I think, 88,000 some dollars

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:36.910
in misappropriated spending.

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:38.670
You just do whatever the (beep) you want

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:41.350
without even asking me, and it's wrong!

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:43.000
- It might surprise you to learn

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:46.540
that Joe's campaign for
Governor of Oklahoma

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:48.660
was not on the up and up.

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:50.620
Under Oklahoma law, you are not allowed

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:53.050
to use corporate funds to fund

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:56.500
an individual run for a political office.

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:59.650
So really, using the funds of the G.W. Zoo

00:17:59.650 --> 00:18:02.300
for his ill-fated campaign for governor

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:04.000
is basically just embezzlement.

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:06.080
In Oklahoma, corporations are prohibited

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:08.450
from making contributions to candidates,

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:10.930
PACs, and party committees,
but they can make

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:13.070
unlimited contributions
to ballot measures.

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:18.070
If Joe in fact did use any
corporate funds of the G.W. Zoo

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:21.543
for his own political
campaign above limits,

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:25.560
definitely a campaign finance violation.

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:29.070
And speaking of Joe's run
for Governor of Oklahoma,

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:31.920
let's talk about his
campaign manager, Josh Dial.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:36.350
- I was Joe's campaign manager
for about a year and a half.

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:39.020
It was the worst experience of my life.

00:18:39.020 --> 00:18:41.150
It was horrible, horrible, horrible.

00:18:41.150 --> 00:18:44.310
- Now although Josh was the
relative voice of reason

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:47.430
throughout this show,
he has a checkered past

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:50.580
including a 2017 felony
assault and battery.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:52.610
The affidavit that was
sworn out against him

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:56.190
states that Dial, "Cut,
stabbed, or slashed,"

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:57.817
I presume his boyfriend,

00:18:57.817 --> 00:19:01.170
"with a Japanese Ninja sword, a katana."

00:19:01.170 --> 00:19:05.520
The victim had an 11 centimeter laceration

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:07.500
and the victim was sent to the hospital

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:09.730
via emergency air evacuation.

00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:11.660
If only there had been a warning sign

00:19:11.660 --> 00:19:13.630
that seemingly normal Josh Dial

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:16.320
might not be as
well-adjusted as we thought.

00:19:16.320 --> 00:19:19.200
- I'm a Libertarian, so
technically (beep) the feds.

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:20.240
- All right, so let's tally up

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:21.760
all the crimes staring with Joe.

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:24.070
He was sentenced to 19 different counts.

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:26.310
His sentence included
108 months for each of

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:29.780
the two murder for hire
counts, totaling 216 months.

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:31.510
He got 12 months for each of the

00:19:31.510 --> 00:19:33.440
Endangered Species Act violations,

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.010
and 14 months for the
Lacey's Act violations,

00:19:36.010 --> 00:19:37.410
all to run concurrently.

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:40.130
Now regarding all of the other
characters in "Tiger King,"

